29,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a sobering reminder that while funding is a flick of a switch, expertise is a slow-growing tree. We have a strong glasshouse crew, but our phenotyping technicians have largely vanished into industry.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems the real cost of research is shifting. While some subsidies remain, shipping and travel costs are eating into the budgets, making it harder for researchers to actually execute their plans.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I've found that our shared tools are in a bit of a mess! The spectroscopy suite was down for weeks because of a lapsed contract, and there aren't enough engineers to go around.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, the repository bottleneck has vanished, but the biological side is far more temperamental. It appears that projects relying on live breeding colonies are significantly more prone to schedule overruns than computational ones.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My research confirms Benjamin's point. Looking at finished awards, those focused on broad catalogues have provided lasting value, whereas high-concept mechanism studies often stalled without resolving their core questions.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, it is a heavy burden when the tools are ready but the hands to guide them are missing. If the engineers are few, we must be cautious about choosing a path that demands constant technical intervention.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I agree. If the budget is being squeezed by rising shipping costs and we lack technical staff, a project that requires constant, expensive logistics or high-maintenance equipment might be too risky.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, that's a great point! If the tools are broken and the money is tight, we should look for something that doesn't need a huge amount of specialized repair work or expensive shipping.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, a delightful realization. If we pair your findings with the schedule overruns I've seen, it seems we should be wary of any proposal that treats biological colonies as a predictable clock.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, exactly. We should prioritize stability over ambition. The data suggests that a project providing a foundational resource is more likely to deliver than one chasing a complex, theoretical mechanism.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, your wisdom on stability is well-placed. Let us seek a project that honors the strength of our remaining crew—perhaps something that leverages the glasshouse—rather than one that relies on the ghosts of technicians past.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, that sounds like a lovely approach. If the glasshouse subsidy is still active, it could provide a stable foundation and help offset some of those rising costs I'm worried about.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I love that idea! If the glasshouse is already doing great and has a good crew, it's way safer than relying on the spectroscopy suite or other broken tools.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, it is a charming coincidence that the glasshouse is both a sanctuary for the plants and a shield for our budget. Let us avoid any ""high-concept"" biological risks that might slip their schedule.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We must avoid the allure of high-concept promises. A project that builds a lasting, usable resource is far more valuable than a theoretical breakthrough that never arrives.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We are in harmony. Let us look for a proposal that is grounded in reality, utilizing our existing strengths and avoiding the fragility of missing expertise or temperamental machinery.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
45,2,4,pass,Servas,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
46,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree completely. Let's prioritize a project that is sustainable and doesn't place an undue burden on the researchers' shrinking budgets or our limited technical staff.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
47,2,4,pass,Midori,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
48,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm totally on board! Let's find a project that's friendly to our staff and doesn't need any fancy tools that might break down. I can't wait to see the candidates!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
49,2,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure to see such a seamless alignment of interests. I shall look forward to seeing which candidate manages to be both scientifically sound and operationally modest.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
51,2,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I concur. The most successful path is one that delivers a tangible asset rather than a promise of discovery. I am ready to review the candidates.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
